        "original_id": "4b1e2646-53cf-517b-a1b6-c19c0a3c5f8e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bryan Brown, John Salthouse, Paul McCartney, Ringo Starr, Peter Webb\n- Films: Breaker Morant, Give My Regards to Broad Street, F/X, Cocktail, Gorillas in the Mist, F/X2, Sweet Talker, Along Came Polly, Australia, Kill Me Three Times, Gods of Egypt, A Bridge Too Far, The Spy Who Loved Me, An American Werewolf in London, Prick Up Your Ears\n- Television: I Didn't Know You Cared, EastEnders, Miracles Take Longer\n- Places: Australia, Britain\n\nFacts:\n- Since the late 1970s, Bryan Brown has performed in more than eighty film and television projects in Australia and abroad.\n- In 1977, John Salthouse appeared in the films A Bridge Too Far and The Spy Who Loved Me.\n- In 1980, Bryan Brown appeared in the film Breaker Morant.\n- In 1981, John Salthouse appeared in the film An American Werewolf in London.\n- In 1984, Give My Regards to Broad Street was released as a British musical drama film directed by Peter Webb and starring Paul McCartney, Bryan Brown, and Ringo Starr.\n- In 1984, Bryan Brown and John Salthouse both appeared in Give My Regards to Broad Street.\n- In 1986, Bryan Brown appeared in the film F/X.\n- In 1987, John Salthouse appeared in the film Prick Up Your Ears.\n- In 1988, Bryan Brown appeared in the films Cocktail and Gorillas in the Mist.\n- In 1991, Bryan Brown appeared in the film F/X2 and starred in the Australian film Sweet Talker.\n- In 2004, Bryan Brown appeared in the film Along Came Polly.\n- In 2008, Bryan Brown appeared in the film Australia.\n- In 2014, Bryan Brown appeared in the film Kill Me Three Times.\n- In 2016, Bryan Brown appeared in the film Gods of Egypt.\n- John Salthouse also appeared in the television series I Didn't Know You Cared, EastEnders, and Miracles Take Longer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
